# codecpack vendored-copy / registry provenance record   (WP112)
#
# tools/codecpacks/<name>.codecpack/ is this repo's working copy of
# codecpacks/<name>/<version>/ in the registry repo. This file records, per
# pack, HOW the two relate, so tools/check-codecpack-sync.sh can tell real
# drift from the two shapes of difference that are not drift.
#
# Read by tools/check-codecpack-sync.sh — keep the two in step.
#
# Format:  <pack>  <mode>  <allowlist>  <gen_macro>
#
#   mode = mirror       the vendored source must be byte-identical to the
#                       registry's. Any difference is drift.
#   mode = fork         the vendored source is intentionally NOT the
#                       registry's: it must be an engine SUPERSET (every
#                       registry code line present; engine-only code allowed).
#   mode = independent  the two are different implementations of the same
#                       job -- neither contains the other, so no containment
#                       question is meaningful. The reason is in this file and
#                       the check prints it on every run.
#
#   allowlist  comma-separated engine-parsed manifest keys whose value may
#              differ from the registry's, each with the reason below.
#              `-` = nothing is excepted.
#   gen_macro  the constant in the pack's source that the manifest's
#              `generation` must equal (`-` if the pack has none). This is
#              checked on EVERY run, registry or not.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (tools/check-codecpack-sync.sh, layers A-C): the two
# repos developed in parallel with nothing cross-checking them, and a
# manifest bug in the registry (qcow2 `map {in}`, missing `decomp_gen`)
# shipped unnoticed because the engine e2e never read the registry's copy.
#
# PROVENANCE, in one paragraph, from `git log -p -- tools/codecpacks/`:
# this repo ORIGINATED the packs (26b0d43, 2026-08-26 .. 23f9db4,
# 2026-09-26) and the registry was seeded from it (2090502, 2026-09-19,
# "seed codecpack registry", whose diff is 11 packs copied out of this tree
# — the registry has no commit older than that one). The vendored copies
# are therefore this repo's development tree, not a third-party import:
# Makefile:169-173 compiles lib<p>.so from the .c next to the manifest,
# Makefile:52 keeps /usr/lib/invfs/codecpacks out of `make test`, and
# Makefile:402 ships the directory in the release tarball.

# --- byte-identical to the registry (raw_image.py, splt.py) ----------------
#  jxl moved OUT of this section in WP-CODECPACK-RESYNC: jxlest.c gained the
#  ADR-007 plugin glue (WP615) and a cmd_estimate()/main() split, so it is a
#  fork now -- the registry copy is exactly the engine copy minus the glue,
#  verified by layer C below. Its manifest `requires = cjxl,djxl` also came
#  back to the registry, which had lost it (the engine probes it; see
#  src/codecs/codec.c:1036).
raw_image    mirror  -           -
splt_test    mirror  -           -

# --- engine ahead: the ADR-007 ivpack plugin glue (WP71, 2a34cd4), which
#     the registry cannot carry (it builds standalone, with no engine
#     headers: registry tools/build-helpers.sh:47). p7z also carries the
#     self_path fallback, rawdisk the fork-window init, xfs the estimate
#     wrapper, ext4fs one memset.
#
#     CORRECTION (2026-10-04). The first version of this comment said "ZERO
#     registry-only code lines in all seven" and described the fork difference
#     as being only plugin glue. That understates vdi and xfs, and the
#     understatement is not cosmetic -- deleting a fork in favour of the
#     registry's copy would SILENTLY REVERT a real fix:
#
#       xfs  registry  #define MAX_MEMBERS 65536u   MAX_IDX 65535u
#            vendored  #define MAX_MEMBERS 1048576u MAX_IDX 1048575u
#       vdi  registry  #define MAP_MAX_ENTS 262148u          <- literal
#            vendored  #define MAP_MAX_ENTS (4u * CPACK_MAX_MEMBERS + 4u)
#
#     That is commit 4db1872, "the 65536 member cap was a RAM bound, not a
#     format limit": a 16x raise of the member bound, plus vdi's derivation
#     turned from a hardcoded literal into a symbolic one so it cannot rot
#     again on the next raise. Neither change reached the registry, so the
#     registry is the STALE side here.
#
#     This corrects a claim in commit f11a8d9's message, which said vdi and xfs
#     were BEHIND the registry because it "has MAP_MAX_ENTS/MAX_MEMBERS/MAX_IDX
#     the vendored copy lacks". Both directions were wrong: those symbols exist
#     on BOTH sides, and the vendored copies are ahead. Published history is
#     left alone rather than rewritten; the measurement above is the record.
#
#     So the registry MUST receive 4db1872 before any fork is deleted, and the
#     plugin glue must land there too -- which is what "reconcile, then move
#     the .so glue so forks are deletable, then delete" means in practice.
ext4fs       fork    -           -
fatfs        fork    -           -
# WP636: engine-originated pack, no registry counterpart yet (layer B/C
# report 'not in the registry (nothing to compare)'); fork records that
# when it lands there the vendored source is the SUPERSET side, as for the
# other engine-first packs. No generation macro: the manifest's
# 'generation = 1' is the only declaration.
iso9660      fork    -           -

# --- WP-CODECPACK-RESYNC: the forks, after the registry was brought up to
#     this tree. Every line above this comment was written when the registry
#     was still missing four things the engine side already had; all four
#     were ported FORWARD (vendored -> registry) by that WP, so the remaining
#     fork delta is the ADR-007 glue and nothing else:
#
#       1. 4db1872's member-bound raise (2^20) and vdi/fatfs's derived
#          MAP_MAX_ENTS, plus rawdisk's hardcoded 65536u in its recipe
#          reader, which outlived the define above it by one bump.
#       2. WP640's ntfs MAX_IMAGE 4 GiB -> 1 TiB.
#       3. WP140's p7z extract_batch (one header parse for the whole member
#          set) and the O(n) kName index that came with it.
#       4. jxlest's cmd_estimate() split (WP615), minus the plugin glue.
#
#     Direction, measured, not assumed: `git -C <registry> diff` on these
#     six packs shows ADDED bound-bump lines on the engine side and none on
#     the registry side, i.e. the registry was STALE, which is what the
#     CORRECTION above says and what the "registry has code the vendored copy
#     lacks" message cannot tell you on its own (it names the direction of
#     the ADDED line, not of the change).
#
#     Each ported file was compiled standalone in the registry's own shape --
#     `cc -std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -c` with no engine headers -- and
#     the registry's `make test` (tools/test-invf-pack.sh) went from 22 passed
#     / 3 failed to 25 passed / 0 failed on the same box: the two ext4fs
#     failures were its sha256 having gone stale when 27f6143 touched
#     ext4fs.c, and the third was p7z's missing `depends = 7zz`.
ntfs         fork    -           -
p7z          fork    -           -
rawdisk      fork    -           -
vdi          fork    -           -
xfs          fork    -           -
# jxl: a codecpack fork, not a mirror any more -- its only delta is the
# ADR-007 glue (the .so export block plus the __has_include chain), because
# jxlest.c is a WP615 plugin target. The shared cmd_estimate() body means the
# CLI and the .so cannot disagree, which is also why the registry copy carries
# that split: layer C compares the two files line by line.
jxl          fork    -           -

# --- qcow2: a real FORK, not staleness. -----------------------------------
# The engine pack and the registry pack are two different designs:
#   engine   generation = 2 (manifest:36) / QCOW2_DECOMP_GEN 2u (qcow2.c:1041),
#            TWO members (diskimg + rankimg), reproduction through the
#            engine's own src/codecs/deflate_repro.h (qcow2.c:151-154) and
#            hence PLUGIN_EXTRA_qcow2 on the link line.
#   registry generation = 3, ONE member, a self-contained QR2 search, no
#            engine dependency.
# Dropping the registry's copy in is a REGRESSION, measured: 28 FAILs in
# tools/test-qcow2.sh ("missing idx 2 rankimg" x11, "strip did not write a
# Q2R3 recipe" on the compressed fixture). Reconciling the two is a design
# WP of its own; until then the two generation numbers MUST NOT be made to
# agree, which is why they are excepted here instead of "fixed".
#
# `map` is excepted for the same reason, and it is the one key in this file
# whose exception is not a lag but a per-implementation ABI pairing:
#   engine   map {recipe} {out} -- cmd_map() loads the Q2R3/Q2R1 RECIPE
#            (qc_map_load, tools/codecpacks/qcow2.codecpack/qcow2.c:1261)
#            because the deflate reproduction parameters only exist there.
#   registry map {in} {out}     -- cmd_map() parses the IMAGE (qc_parse,
#            codecpacks/qcow2/1.0.0/qcow2.c) and re-derives the layout from
#            the L1/L2 tables, which is what its one-member design allows.
# The engine passes BOTH operands and the manifest template decides which one
# the pack is handed (src/core/vol_cpack.c:4706-4715 spells the rule out and
# names qcow2 as the case that needs {recipe}); each manifest is therefore
# correct for its own source, and forcing either value on the other side
# breaks that side's map. `decomp_gen` is NOT excepted: the registry copy
# renders a v1 MRMP map, so declaring it is inert now and correct if the map
# ever becomes v2 (src/core/vol_cpack.c:4721 stamps only an MRM2 header).
qcow2        independent  generation,pack_version,map  QCOW2_DECOMP_GEN

# --- wim: engine-ORIGINATED, the registry has no copy at all. --------------
# WP637 vendored this pack here first; the registry was seeded from this tree
# (see PROVENANCE above) and has never carried wim, so layers B and C have
# nothing to compare and layer A only checks that the manifest generation
# agrees with the source (it carries no GEN macro: the pack is verbatim, it
# re-encodes nothing, so there is no decomposition generation to bump).
# Its one real bug so far is recorded where the format is: wim.c's header
# comment, 56/8/56 -- the lane declined every real WIM until WP637 fixed the
# resource-header parse, and the fixtures had been written from the same
# misreading, which is why no sync check could ever have caught it.
wim          independent  -           -

# --- png: engine-ORIGINATED, byte-exact PNG recompression via png2jxl + preflate.
png          independent  -           -

